Notebook[{
 Cell["Independent direct five-dimensional Wald--Tachikawa entropy audit", "Title"],
 Cell["Fresh reconstruction from the near-horizon metric, the certified corrected fields, and the form-action coefficient", "Subtitle"],
 Cell["Scope", "Section"],
 Cell["This notebook is an independent audit. It reconstructs the horizon-adapted frame and normal-bundle connection from the coordinate metric. It does not import or evaluate the candidate entropy notebook. The active invariant is lambda3 L4^(3), and P=mu1 mu2 mu3.", "Text"],
 Cell["The oriented mostly-plus frame has the flat-index symbol epsilonLower[0,1,2,3,4]=+1 and epsilonUpper[0,1,2,3,4]=-1. The curved tensor is its five-vielbein transform and carries the determinant. The BMPV base orientation makes (t,r,theta,phi,psi) orientation reversing, so its curved components are coordinate epsilonLower=-Sqrt[-g] epsilonTilde and coordinate epsilonUpper=+epsilonTilde/Sqrt[-g]. Mathematica's positive alternating density is epsilonTilde, and the physical induced horizon orientation is -sigma1 wedge sigma2 wedge sigma3. The positive BMPV gauge potentials follow Eq. 4.1 of arXiv:2603.18180.", "Text"],
 Cell[BoxData["alt5=Normal[LeviCivitaTensor[5]]; frameEpsilonLowerOrdered=1; frameEpsilonUpperOrdered=-1; coordinateOrientation=-1; coordinateEpsilonLowerSign=-1; coordinateEpsilonUpperSign=1; actionArrayOrdered=alt5[[1,2,3,4,5]]; epsilonConventionPass=TrueQ[{frameEpsilonLowerOrdered,frameEpsilonUpperOrdered,coordinateOrientation,coordinateEpsilonLowerSign,coordinateEpsilonUpperSign,actionArrayOrdered}=={1,-1,-1,-1,1,1}]; Print[<|\"FlatSymbolLower01234\"->frameEpsilonLowerOrdered,\"FlatSymbolUpper01234\"->frameEpsilonUpperOrdered,\"CurvedCoordinateLowerSign\"->coordinateEpsilonLowerSign,\"CurvedCoordinateUpperSign\"->coordinateEpsilonUpperSign,\"AlternatingDensity\"->actionArrayOrdered,\"Pass\"->epsilonConventionPass|>];"], "Input"],
 Cell[BoxData["ClearAll[P,mu1,mu2,mu3,j,gap,G5,S0,assumptions];\nP=mu1 mu2 mu3; gap=P-j^2; assumptions=mu1>0&&mu2>0&&mu3>0&&G5>0&&0<=j^2<P;\nS0=Pi^2 Sqrt[gap]/(2G5);"], "Input"],
 Cell["1. Near-horizon coordinate geometry", "Section"],
 Cell["The near-horizon metric is obtained directly from H_I=1+mu_I/r^2 and the BMPV one-form omega=j sigma3/(2r^2). The coordinate order is (t,r,theta,phi,psi), with sigma3=dpsi+cos(theta)dphi.", "Text"],
 Cell[BoxData["coords={t,r,th,ph,ps}; n=Length[coords];\na=P^(1/3)/4; b=gap/(4P^(2/3));\ng=ConstantArray[0,{n,n}];\ng[[1,1]]=-r^4/P^(2/3); g[[2,2]]=P^(1/3)/r^2; g[[3,3]]=a;\ng[[1,4]]=g[[4,1]]=-j r^2 Cos[th]/(2P^(2/3));\ng[[1,5]]=g[[5,1]]=-j r^2/(2P^(2/3));\ng[[4,4]]=a Sin[th]^2+b Cos[th]^2; g[[4,5]]=g[[5,4]]=b Cos[th]; g[[5,5]]=b;\ngInv=FullSimplify[Inverse[g],Assumptions->assumptions&&r>0&&0<th<Pi];\nchrist=Table[1/2 Sum[gInv[[aa,dd]](D[g[[dd,cc]],coords[[bb]]]+D[g[[dd,bb]],coords[[cc]]]-D[g[[bb,cc]],coords[[dd]]]),{dd,n}],{aa,n},{bb,n},{cc,n}];\nRup=Table[FullSimplify[D[christ[[aa,dd,bb]],coords[[cc]]]-D[christ[[aa,cc,bb]],coords[[dd]]]+Sum[christ[[aa,cc,ee]]christ[[ee,dd,bb]]-christ[[aa,dd,ee]]christ[[ee,cc,bb]],{ee,n}],Assumptions->assumptions&&r>0&&0<th<Pi],{aa,n},{bb,n},{cc,n},{dd,n}];\nRdown=Table[FullSimplify[Sum[g[[aa,ee]]Rup[[ee,bb,cc,dd]],{ee,n}],Assumptions->assumptions&&r>0&&0<th<Pi],{aa,n},{bb,n},{cc,n},{dd,n}];"], "Input"],
 Cell["The raw orthonormal duals E0,E1,E4 and the constant horizon boost are constructed independently. The adapted timelike normal is E0p=gamma(E0+u E4).", "Text"],
 Cell[BoxData["E0={P^(1/3)/r^2,0,0,0,0}; E1={0,r/P^(1/6),0,0,0}; E4={-j/(r^2 P^(1/6)),0,0,0,2/P^(1/6)};\nprojR[v1_,v2_,v3_,v4_]:=FullSimplify[Sum[Rdown[[aa,bb,cc,dd]]v1[[aa]]v2[[bb]]v3[[cc]]v4[[dd]],{aa,n},{bb,n},{cc,n},{dd,n}],Assumptions->assumptions&&r>0&&0<th<Pi];\nrawR0101=projR[E0,E1,E0,E1]; rawR4101=projR[E4,E1,E0,E1]; rawR4141=projR[E4,E1,E4,E1];\nu=j/Sqrt[P]; gamma=Sqrt[P/gap]; E0p=FullSimplify[gamma(E0+u E4),Assumptions->assumptions];\nadaptedR=projR[E0p,E1,E0p,E1];\ngeometryRPass=TrueQ[FullSimplify[{rawR0101-(j^2+4P)/P^(4/3),rawR4101+4j/P^(5/6),rawR4141-3j^2/P^(4/3),adaptedR-(4P-3j^2)/P^(4/3)},Assumptions->assumptions]==ConstantArray[0,4]];\nPrint[<|\"RawR0101\"->Factor[rawR0101],\"RawR4101\"->Factor[rawR4101],\"RawR4141\"->Factor[rawR4141],\"AdaptedR\"->Factor[adaptedR],\"Pass\"->geometryRPass|>];"], "Input"],
 Cell["2. Field strengths and covariant Wald kernel", "Section"],
 Cell[BoxData["rawF01=-2P^(1/6)/{mu1,mu2,mu3}; rawF41=2j/(P^(1/3){mu1,mu2,mu3});\nadaptedF=FullSimplify[gamma(rawF01+u rawF41),Assumptions->assumptions];\nXup=P^(1/3)/{mu1,mu2,mu3}; Xdown={mu1,mu2,mu3}/(3P^(1/3)); lambdaDirection={0,0,1};\nDij=Table[3lambdaDirection[[ii]]Xdown[[kk]]-(9/2)Xup[[3]]Xdown[[ii]]Xdown[[kk]],{ii,3},{kk,3}];\nwaldKernel=FullSimplify[Xup[[3]]adaptedR+1/2 Sum[Dij[[ii,kk]]adaptedF[[ii]]adaptedF[[kk]],{ii,3},{kk,3}],Assumptions->assumptions];\nwaldRelative=-4 waldKernel; covariantPass=TrueQ[FullSimplify[{adaptedF+2Sqrt[gap]/(P^(1/3){mu1,mu2,mu3}),waldKernel-1/mu3,waldRelative+4/mu3},Assumptions->assumptions]=={ConstantArray[0,3],0,0}];\nPrint[<|\"AdaptedF01\"->Factor[adaptedF],\"WaldKernel\"->Factor[waldKernel],\"RelativeEntropyCoefficient\"->Factor[waldRelative],\"Pass\"->covariantPass|>];"], "Input"],
 Cell["3. Normal-bundle connection from the same coordinate metric", "Section"],
 Cell["The coframe and dual frame are supplied explicitly. The spin connection is omega^a_b=e^a_mu (d E_b^mu+Gamma^mu_nu E_b^nu). Tachikawa's Gamma_N=-epsilon^mu_nu Gamma^nu_mu/2 is evaluated in the boosted normal frame.", "Text"],
 Cell[BoxData["coE0={r^2/P^(1/3),0,0,j Cos[th]/(2P^(1/3)),j/(2P^(1/3))}; coE1={0,P^(1/6)/r,0,0,0}; coE4={0,0,0,P^(1/6)Cos[th]/2,P^(1/6)/2};\ncoE0p=FullSimplify[gamma(coE0-u coE4),Assumptions->assumptions];\nspin[aCov_,bVec_,mu_]:=FullSimplify[Sum[aCov[[nu]](D[bVec[[nu]],coords[[mu]]]+Sum[christ[[nu,mu,rho]]bVec[[rho]],{rho,n}]),{nu,n}],Assumptions->assumptions&&r>0&&0<th<Pi];\nomegaUp0Down1=Table[spin[coE0p,E1,mu],{mu,n}];\n(* For epsilon_01=+1 in mostly-plus signature, Tachikawa Gamma_N=-epsilon^a_b omega^b_a/2=omega^0_1. *)\nGammaN=FullSimplify[omegaUp0Down1,Assumptions->assumptions&&r>0&&0<th<Pi];\ngammaNCoefficient=FullSimplify[GammaN[[5]],Assumptions->assumptions];\nGammaNPullback=GammaN[[{3,4,5}]]; gammaNFormPass=TrueQ[FullSimplify[GammaNPullback-gammaNCoefficient{0,Cos[th],1},Assumptions->assumptions&&r>0&&0<th<Pi]==ConstantArray[0,3]];\nPrint[<|\"GammaNFullComponents\"->Factor[GammaN],\"HorizonPullback\"->Factor[GammaNPullback],\"Sigma3Coefficient\"->Factor[gammaNCoefficient],\"HopfPullbackPass\"->gammaNFormPass|>];"], "Input"],
 Cell["4. Mixed Chern--Simons coefficient and orientation", "Section"],
 Cell["The Lorentz matrix trace is tr(R wedge R)=R^a_b wedge R^b_a=-(1/4) R_{mu nu rho sigma} R_{alpha beta}^{rho sigma} dx^{mu nu alpha beta}. Because the notebook chart reverses the physical orientation, the scalar component term +(lambda3/(2 e)) epsilonTilde R R A, with epsilonTilde the alternating coordinate density, is the oriented form +2 lambda3 A3 wedge tr(R wedge R). Equivalently, the density e L has coefficient +(lambda3/2). The physical Tachikawa formula is +(lambda3/G5) Integral_phys Gamma_N wedge F3. The induced horizon orientation gives Integral_phys[sigma3 wedge d sigma3]=+16 Pi^2. The simultaneous form-sign and horizon-orientation corrections preserve the numerical entropy.", "Text"],
 Cell[BoxData["f3Hopf=j/(2mu3); hopfIntegral=16Pi^2;\nnormalIntegral=FullSimplify[gammaNCoefficient f3Hopf hopfIntegral,Assumptions->assumptions];\ncsEntropyCoefficient=FullSimplify[normalIntegral/G5,Assumptions->assumptions];\ncsRelative=FullSimplify[csEntropyCoefficient/S0,Assumptions->assumptions];\ncsPass=TrueQ[FullSimplify[csRelative-8j^2/(P mu3),Assumptions->assumptions]==0];\nPrint[<|\"PhysicalIntegralGammaNWedgeF3\"->Factor[normalIntegral],\"RelativeEntropyCoefficient\"->Factor[csRelative],\"Pass\"->csPass|>];"], "Input"],
 Cell["5. Corrected horizon area", "Section"],
 Cell["The next cell embeds only the three metric corrections Ft,K,Om extracted from the independently EOM-certified notebook 11. The embedded expressions are not read from the candidate entropy notebook.", "Text"],
 Cell[BoxData["metricFields=<|\"Ft\"->(-4*(24*q1^3*q2^3*q3^3+29*q1^3*q2^3*q3^2*x+65*q1^3*q2^2*q3^3*x+65*q1^2*q2^3*q3^3*x+4*q1^3*q2^3*q3*x^2+74*q1^3*q2^2*q3^2*x^2+74*q1^2*q2^3*q3^2*x^2+64*q1^3*q2*q3^3*x^2+170*q1^2*q2^2*q3^3*x^2+64*q1*q2^3*q3^3*x^2+6*q1^3*q2^2*q3*x^3+6*q1^2*q2^3*q3*x^3+78*q1^3*q2*q3^2*x^3+165*q1^2*q2^2*q3^2*x^3+78*q1*q2^3*q3^2*x^3+24*q1^3*q3^3*x^3+162*q1^2*q2*q3^3*x^3+162*q1*q2^2*q3^3*x^3+24*q2^3*q3^3*x^3+16*q1^3*q2*q3*x^4-24*q1^2*q2^2*q3*x^4+16*q1*q2^3*q3*x^4+36*q1^3*q3^2*x^4+156*q1^2*q2*q3^2*x^4+156*q1*q2^2*q3^2*x^4+36*q2^3*q3^2*x^4+60*q1^2*q3^3*x^4+148*q1*q2*q3^3*x^4+60*q2^2*q3^3*x^4+5*q1^3*q2*x^5-10*q1^2*q2^2*x^5+5*q1*q2^3*x^5+17*q1^3*q3*x^5-21*q1^2*q2*q3*x^5-21*q1*q2^2*q3*x^5+17*q2^3*q3*x^5+74*q1^2*q3^2*x^5+123*q1*q2*q3^2*x^5+74*q2^2*q3^2*x^5+53*q1*q3^3*x^5+53*q2*q3^3*x^5+6*q1^3*x^6-6*q1^2*q2*x^6-6*q1*q2^2*x^6+6*q2^3*x^6+18*q1^2*q3*x^6-48*q1*q2*q3*x^6+18*q2^2*q3*x^6+54*q1*q3^2*x^6+54*q2*q3^2*x^6+18*q3^3*x^6+7*q1^2*x^7-14*q1*q2*x^7+7*q2^2*x^7-2*q1*q3*x^7-2*q2*q3*x^7+19*q3^2*x^7))/(3*x*(q1+x)^2*(q2+x)^2*(q3+x)^3*(q1*q2+q1*q3+q2*q3+2*q1*x+2*q2*x+2*q3*x+3*x^2))-(8*jrot^2*(6*q1*q2*q3+7*(q1*q2+q1*q3+q2*q3)*x+8*(q1+q2+q3)*x^2+9*x^3))/(x*(q1+x)*(q2+x)*(q3+x)^2*((q1+x)*(q2+x)+(q1+x)*(q3+x)+(q2+x)*(q3+x))),\"K\"->0,\"Om\"->(4*jrot*(12*q1^2*q2^2*q3^2+22*q1^2*q2^2*q3*x+40*q1^2*q2*q3^2*x+40*q1*q2^2*q3^2*x+6*q1^2*q2^2*x^2+63*q1^2*q2*q3*x^2+63*q1*q2^2*q3*x^2+27*q1^2*q3^2*x^2+102*q1*q2*q3^2*x^2+27*q2^2*q3^2*x^2+15*q1^2*q2*x^3+15*q1*q2^2*x^3+39*q1^2*q3*x^3+144*q1*q2*q3*x^3+39*q2^2*q3*x^3+60*q1*q3^2*x^3+60*q2*q3^2*x^3+8*q1^2*x^4+26*q1*q2*x^4+8*q2^2*x^4+77*q1*q3*x^4+77*q2*q3*x^4+32*q3^2*x^4+9*q1*x^5+9*q2*x^5+36*q3*x^5))/(3*x^2*(q1+x)*(q2+x)*(q3+x)^2*(q1*q2+q1*q3+q2*q3+2*q1*x+2*q2*x+2*q3*x+3*x^2))+(24*jrot^3)/(x^2*(q3+x)*((q1+x)*(q2+x)+(q1+x)*(q3+x)+(q2+x)*(q3+x)))|>;"], "Input"],
 Cell[BoxData["productD=(x+mu1)(x+mu2)(x+mu3); areaBase=productD^(1/3); fiberBase=areaBase-j^2/productD^(2/3);\nhorizonShift=16(3j^2+2P)/(mu3(mu1 mu2+mu1 mu3+mu2 mu3)); f0=Log[x]-Log[productD]/3; omega0=j/(2x);\nfC=metricFields[\"Ft\"]/.{q1->mu1,q2->mu2,q3->mu3,jrot->j}; fC=fC+horizonShift D[f0,x];\nomegaC=metricFields[\"Om\"]/.{q1->mu1,q2->mu2,q3->mu3,jrot->j}; omegaC=omegaC+horizonShift D[omega0,x];\nkC=metricFields[\"K\"]/.{q1->mu1,q2->mu2,q3->mu3,jrot->j};\nbaseCorrection=horizonShift D[areaBase,x];\nfiberCorrection=Together[baseCorrection+2areaBase kC-4(x^2/productD^(2/3))omega0^2(2fC+2omegaC/omega0)];\nareaRelative=FullSimplify[Limit[baseCorrection/areaBase+fiberCorrection/(2fiberBase),x->0,Direction->\"FromAbove\"],Assumptions->assumptions];\nareaExpected=4(2j^4-7j^2 P+4P^2)/(P mu3 gap); areaPass=TrueQ[FullSimplify[areaRelative-areaExpected,Assumptions->assumptions]==0];\nPrint[<|\"RelativeAreaCoefficient\"->Factor[areaRelative],\"Pass\"->areaPass|>];"], "Input"],
 Cell["6. Independent verdict", "Section"],
 Cell[BoxData["surfaceRelative=FullSimplify[waldRelative+csRelative,Assumptions->assumptions]; totalRelative=FullSimplify[areaRelative+surfaceRelative,Assumptions->assumptions];\nsurfaceExpected=4(2j^2-P)/(P mu3); totalExpected=4(3P-4j^2)/(mu3 gap); totalPass=TrueQ[FullSimplify[{surfaceRelative-surfaceExpected,totalRelative-totalExpected},Assumptions->assumptions]=={0,0}];\nPrint[<|\"Area\"->Factor[areaRelative],\"CovariantWald\"->Factor[waldRelative],\"MixedCS\"->Factor[csRelative],\"SurfaceTotal\"->Factor[surfaceRelative],\"GrandTotal\"->Factor[totalRelative]|>];\nFinalAuditAssociation=<|\"LeviCivitaAndChartOrientationPass\"->epsilonConventionPass,\"GeometryRiemannPass\"->geometryRPass,\"CovariantKernelPass\"->covariantPass,\"NormalConnectionHopfPullbackPass\"->gammaNFormPass,\"MixedCSPass\"->csPass,\"CorrectedAreaPass\"->areaPass,\"TotalPass\"->totalPass,\"CSRelative\"->Factor[csRelative],\"TotalRelative\"->Factor[totalRelative]|>; FinalPass=And@@Cases[Values[FinalAuditAssociation],True|False]; Print[FinalAuditAssociation]; Print[<|\"FINAL_PASS\"->FinalPass|>];"], "Input"]
}, WindowTitle->"Independent direct 5D entropy audit", StyleDefinitions->"Default.nb"]
